  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 537756,
  "published": "2026-10-09T21:16:33.16Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.6.1: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.6.1\n\nv0.6.0: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.6.0 (qubit limits come from the backend; see its notes)\n\nv0.5.2: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.5.2\n\nv0.5.1: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.5.1\n- ADDED: the backend reports its device's qubits (IQubitLimitedBackend, Braket.Devices.maxQubits) for the devices the module names\n- ADDED: BraketBackend takes maxQubits, which replaces that figure; BraketBackend.CreateWithDeviceLimitAsync and deviceQubitsAsync read the device's own qubit count (GetDevice, Braket.Devices.qubitCountOfCapabilities)\n\nv0.5.0: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.5.0 (Task-based API; see its notes)\n\nv0.4.16: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.16\n- CHANGED: Braket results carry their recorded counts, so measuring a returned state yields Braket's own shots rather than outcomes resampled from its amplitudes\n\nv0.4.14: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.14\n- ADDED: the Braket backend implements IShotSamplingBackend, so sampled UCCSD-VQE knows its shot count\n- CHANGED: circuits are transpiled to the target device's gate set before OpenQASM 3.0 export, so composite gates (Toffoli, multi-controlled, controlled-phase) reach the device; an optional JobBudget limits submitted jobs\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.14+",
